; An element of a uniform-space var passed as a reference from
; GPU-reachable code: rejected by the context-exclusivity pass. A
; whole-global ref (a bare name) is legal everywhere — the reference
; monomorphizer inlines the specific global in place of the parameter,
; pinned by the `storage_ref_gpu` success test — but an accessor-chain
; ref into a uniform/storage var becomes a real pointer parameter, which
; base WGSL only allows in the function/private address spaces.
; Read-only `@ref`, so this pins the reference rule itself — a mutable
; ref would trip the illegal-GPU-write validation first. The same call
; in cpu/audio-only code is legal — pinned by the `storage_ref_cpu` cpu
; test.
@uniform
(var uniform-floats: [4: f32])

@storage-write
(var out: [1: f32])

(defn get-it [@ref x: f32]: f32
  x)

(defn f []: f32
  (get-it (uniform-floats 0u)))

@compute
(defn entry []
  (= (out 0u) (f)))
